<title>GERMANY: German trader sees 850,000 T main Ivory cocoa crop.</title>
<headline>German trader sees 850,000 T main Ivory cocoa crop.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cocoa trader Albrecht &amp; Dill in its weekly market report said it was assuming an Ivorian 1996/97 main crop of around 850,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Latest information received from pod-counters made a late start to the harvest look unlikely, A&amp;D said.</p>
<p>A&amp;D also said the European industry used recent price lows to take some cover but there was little origin selling.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
